	(text "# POWER SUPPLY SUBSYSTEM DESIGN NOTES (REGULATOR BLOCK)\nProject: OpenMycoNet BLE_BRIDGE\nStatus: READY FOR MANUFACTURING (JLCPCB 4-Layer Stackup)\nDate: 2026-10-25\nRevision: 2.3\n\nSYSTEM OVERVIEW\nThe power supply subsystem utilizes two independent TPS63020DSJR buck-boost converters to separate the digital core from sensitive analog measurement blocks.\nDual converters prevent high-frequency digital switching noise and transient load ripples from degrading precision sensor readings and ADC reference baselines.\n\n1. DIGITAL POWER RAIL SETUP (+3.3V / +3.3VD)\n• Converter IC: U2 (TPS63020DSJR high-efficiency buck-boost converter).\n• Function: Regulates variable VDD input (USB 5V or LiPo battery 3.0V-4.2V) to a stable +3.3V digital supply rail.\n• Input Decoupling: C2 (10 µF), C3 (10 µF), and C4 (100 nF) MLCC ceramic capacitors placed close to pins VIN_10, VIN_11, and VINA.\n• Feedback Network: Voltage divider using R6 (1 MΩ) and R7 (180 kΩ) tied to Pin 3 (FB) sets output regulation to +3.28V:\n  V_OUT = 0.5 V × (1 + 1 M / 180 k) = 3.278 V ≈ 3.30 V.\n• Output Filtering: Main digital output is filtered by C5 (10 µF) ceramic capacitor.\n• Power Good Monitor: Pin 14 (PG) pulled up to VOUT through R5 (100 kΩ).\n• Power Inductor: L1 (1.5 µH) connected across switching terminals L1 (Pins 8, 9) and L2 (Pins 6, 7).\n• Control Pins: EN (Pin 12) tied to VDD and PS/SYNC (Pin 13) grounded for continuous forced PWM active-mode operation.\n\n2. CLEAN ANALOG POWER RAIL SETUP (+3.3VA)\n• Converter IC: U3 (TPS63020DSJR high-efficiency buck-boost converter).\n• Function: Regulates variable VDD input into an isolated, ultra-clean +3.3VA supply rail for the analog front-end (OPA2320S, INA333, ADS1115 ADCs).\n• Input Decoupling: C6 (10 µF), C7 (10 µF), and C8 (100 nF) ceramic capacitors connected across VIN_10, VIN_11, and VINA.\n• Feedback Network: Voltage divider using R9 (1 MΩ) and R10 (180 kΩ) tied to Pin 3 (FB) sets analog rail regulation to +3.28V:\n  V_OUT = 0.5 V × (1 + 1 M / 180 k) = 3.278 V ≈ 3.30 V.\n• Output Filtering: Low-pass output filtering provided by C9 (10 µF) ceramic capacitor.\n• Power Good Monitor: Pin 14 (PG) pulled up to VOUT through R8 (100 kΩ).\n• Power Inductor: L2 (1.5 µH) connected across switching terminals L1 (Pins 8, 9) and L2 (Pins 6, 7).\n• Control Pins: EN (Pin 12) tied to VDD and PS/SYNC (Pin 13) grounded for low-noise continuous mode operation.\n\n3. GROUND PLANE & RULE VERIFICATION SETUP\n• Common System Ground (GND): Solid common ground return plane utilized across all 4 layers under Revision 2.3 to eliminate loop antennas and return-path discontinuities.\n• PWR_FLAG: Tied directly to the power rails and GND nets on both U2 and U3 output domains for automated KiCad Electrical Rules Check (ERC) power-driver verification."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 13.462 48.768 0)
		(effects
